In article <1991Nov05.071000.25763@frodo.cc.flinders.edu.au>, majwr@cc.flinders.edu.au (J.W.Rice) writes:
|> Can someone tell me what system shocks are, what causes them, and how to
|> prevent them?
|> I was killed by one on Level One whilst wearing a ring of polymorph and a cloak
|> of magic resistance.
|> 		Benno.

System shocks (naturally) are a part of the AD&D game system.  They occur for
a number of reasons, including polymorphing.  The chance to survive is based
on your CON score.  Don't wear that ring unless you have a ring of polymorph
control, then change into the monster of your choice and take the ring off,
especially if you don't have a high Constitution.  Changing as a lycanthrope
(were-xxxx) is o.k. though.
